			"author": {
				"name": "Stéphane Deschamps",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@accessiblestef",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/770/108/129/802/original/98f5333c1cd98a89.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-12-02T16:20:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I guess you're probably 50% tongue in cheek here, but I'd venture to ask nonetheless:<br>I'd make a difference between web sites (content) and web apps; the former is for consumption on display of the page and is then usually (hopefully) cached by the browser and/or retrieved by tools like pocket, wallabag etc., the latter needs to handle actions as an offline feature to be updated when it has the chance to do so.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109445241597881549",
			"parentId": "109444991481168197",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109445241597881549",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-12-02T17:24:15.441Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@accessiblestef\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>accessiblestef</span></a></span> I think this one was probably 80 or 90% tongue-in-cheek. I do think offline sites are valuable but to me it’s a “code smell”-esque issue when we have to bifurcate entire properties into sites versus apps for technical reasons. I think that bifurcation should be done at the smaller component/module/design block level</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
